          "id": "60c47792e4ee5c767879ab34b4ccf1807094a91e",
          "message": "feat(vector): add vector scan telemetry and read-only diagnostics (#6178)\n\n# Vector scan telemetry and read-only diagnostics\n\nInstrumentation and diagnostics only; no scoring, build, or planning\nchanges.\n\n## Telemetry\n\n`io_stats` supplies per-component IO for every query type and a\nper-stage overlay\nfor vector scans under `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, VERBOSE)`. Collection is gated\nat runtime\non an active instrumentation request: ordinary text and vector reads\nbypass buffer\nsnapshots and string/map accounting, even when the feature is compiled\nin.\nScoped guards cover executor initialization, execution, rescan, and\nparallel DSM\ncallbacks, restoring the prior state on nesting or unwinding.\n\nVector timings include `scan_init`, `non_vector_search`, routing, layer\nscans and\nboundaries, and reranking. Parallel-worker counters aggregate without\nsumming\nconcurrent worker durations.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> Text queries never acquire vector stage labels. Instrumented text\nqueries gain\n> only additive per-component IO rows.\n\n## Diagnostics\n\n- `paradedb.vector_info` distinguishes configured policy\n(`configured_quantized`,\n`configured_layers`, `configured_bytes_per_row`, `configured_format`)\nfrom\n`quantized_storage`, the actual presence of quantized slots in each\nsegment.\nA configured field can therefore correctly report no codes in a flat\nsegment.\n- `paradedb.vector_estimator_info(index, field[, queries])` reports\nper-layer\nestimator bias and spread using sampled pseudo-queries or supplied\n`vector[]`.\n  It is deterministic, snapshot-aware, read-only, and persists nothing.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> The diagnostic measures the index; it never calibrates or changes\nserving behavior.\n\nDocs: *Diagnosing Quantized Vector Indexes*. Schema fragment:\n`pg_search/sql/unreleased/6178.vector_estimator_info.sql`.\n\n## Review verification\n\n`ordinary_reads_bypass_collection_and_reader_open_snapshots` and\n`instrumentation_request_restores_nested_state_and_unwinds` cover the\nruntime gate.\nThe `vector_quantized_storage` SQL regression covers a mixed flat/IVF\nindex with\nthe same configured policy and different actual code presence. The\nquantization\nSQL matrix covers estimator behavior and diagnostic errors.\n\nAll 344 PostgreSQL 18 regression tests passed locally on the\ncurrent-main rebase.\nSchema CI, docs, PostgreSQL 15–18 system tests, and upgrades from 0.21.0\nand 0.25.6\nalso pass.\n\n### Ordinary-query feature cost\n\nApple M5, PostgreSQL 18.3, release builds from the same PR head, shared\n1M `[1,4]`\nindex (d=1024), one client/worker, prepared statements, warm cache, no\nEXPLAIN.\nText is a score-ordered top-10 search for `history`; vector is one fixed\nheld-out\nquery, cosine top-10, probe 0.0109, depth 2. Each round has 200 warmup\nexecutions\nper query type followed by three 1,000-transaction measured batches. Run\norder:\nfeature on → off → on again. Table values are means of the reported\nbatch means\n(six on batches, three off); ranges show run-to-run variation.\n\n| Plain query | `io_stats` off, ms (range) | `io_stats` on, ms (range) |\nObserved on − off |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Text | 0.1407 (0.139–0.143) | 0.1493 (0.146–0.152) | +0.0087 ms /\n+6.2% |\n| Vector | 3.0963 (3.081–3.106) | 3.1345 (3.069–3.193) | +0.0382 ms /\n+1.2% |\n\nThese are narrow local measurements, not a zero-overhead claim. The\nrepeated\nfeature-on vector batches averaged 3.086 ms, overlapping the off result;\nthe\nvector difference is sensitive to run order. Runtime gating removes\ncollection\nand snapshots, not all compiled feature branches. Raw pgbench output is\npreserved\nunder `pdbench/runs/review-fixes-20260907/plain-query-cost/`.\n\nFollow-ups: centroid-relative L2 scoring for offset-heavy data remains\nin the\nTantivy scan review; the reviewer still needs pdbench access to review\nthe compare\nimplementation and HTML reports. The 10M discriminator is deferred; new\nbenchmark\nverification uses only 1M data. The existing shared `[1,4]` index is\ncompatible;\nthe older `[1,1]` index has V2 centroids and needs a separate\nV3-compatible copy\nbefore it can be tested with current main.\n\nPins tantivy `53d2b7682df4b275629a3e4be3538d7d459d8b16`.\n\nInherits the direct training options from #6177: `training_sample_ratio\n= 0.32` and `max_leaf_size = 100`. Diagnostic fixtures use the new\noption names.\n\nRebased with #6177 onto main `cd3451c19143d0106c6e7a2cb5656245df8d423f`\n(#6432 and #6433), retaining shared RNG router setup on every index\nopen. Validation includes PostgreSQL 18 `vector_merge`,\n`vector_training_options`, `vector_quantization`,\n`vector_quantized_storage`, and `vector_delete_all_docs`, plus pg_search\nclippy, nightly Rust formatting, and Prettier.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-bot[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-bot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Walter Woodall <wwoodal@paradedb.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
