          "id": "23148823004c1fbab188a03c8ce5e05a6fc8e590",
          "message": "feat: hand training vectors to superkmeans by value to halve training memory (#5776)\n\nPart of #5770.\n\nIVF centroid training kept two full copies of the sampled training set\nresident: tantivy's sample buffer plus superkmeans' rotated copy, alive\nthrough all three hierarchical phases (~2 × 0.32·n·d·4 bytes with\ndefault settings). The clusterer now receives the training buffer owned\nand superkmeans rotates it in place block-wise, so peak training memory\nis one copy.\n\nDepends on branch pins (draft until they merge and revs are re-pinned):\n- paradedb/tantivy#191 — `IvfClusterer::train` takes owned\n`IvfTrainingVectors`\n- paradedb/superkmeans-rs#16 — `train_owned` + in-place rotation\n\nNo behavior change: identical GEMM, parity-tested borrowed vs owned in\nsuperkmeans-rs.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: paradedb-github-app[bot] <282009505+paradedb-github-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-08-03T19:30:02Z",
